{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/orderedcollections\/orderedset\/elements"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"elements","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:18OrderedCollections0A3SetV7Elementxmfp","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"] { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is possible to mutate the set by updating the value of this property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This guarantees that direct mutations happen in place when possible (i.e.,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without spurious copy-on-write copies).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"However, the set needs to ensure the uniqueness of its members, so every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"update to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements"},{"type":"text","text":" includes a postprocessing step to detect and remove"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duplicates over the entire array. This can be slower than doing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equivalent updates with direct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrderedSet"},{"type":"text","text":" operations, so updating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements"},{"type":"text","text":" is best used in cases where direct implementations aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available – for example, when you need to call a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableCollection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm that isn’t directly implemented by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrderedSet"},{"type":"text","text":" itself."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1) for the getter. Mutating this property has an expected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complexity of O(","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), if ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements high-quality hashing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:18OrderedCollections0A3SetV8elementsSayxGvp","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"modules":[{"name":"OrderedCollections"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","extendedModule":"OrderedCollections","role":"symbol","title":"elements","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"elements","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:18OrderedCollections0A3SetV7Elementxmfp"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.SwiftyLab.HelperCoders\/documentation\/OrderedCollections\/OrderedSet\/elements","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.SwiftyLab.HelperCoders\/documentation\/OrderedCollections","doc:\/\/com.SwiftyLab.HelperCoders\/documentation\/OrderedCollections\/OrderedSet"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A view of the members of this set, as a regular array value."}],"references":{"doc://com.SwiftyLab.HelperCoders/documentation/OrderedCollec